sec.p:
Telemetry and control messages are protected with AES-GCM. Associated data contains SID, sequence number, message type, and policy epoch. The UCC maintains authoritative replay state, while the DCU may maintain a coarse cache and rate-control state. This design binds identity, role, ephemeral key contributions, freshness, policy context, and the application key to one authenticated session transcript. In Eqs. (5)–(8), SIT_SM is the meter credential, Sign_SK_UCC denotes signing with SK_UCC, H is the hash function, TR is the authenticated transcript digest, N_SM/N_UCC are nonces, SID is the session identifier, PolicyEpoch is the current policy version, and Auth_SM/Auth_UCC are role-specific key-confirmation tags; 

    ‖

 denotes concatenation.
